Description: NETINSIGHT common files (units, conf, logrotate, AppArmor, installer)
 Shared assets needed by every NETINSIGHT install: systemd unit files,
 logrotate configuration, AppArmor profile, the sanitised configuration
 template, alembic.ini, the permission-catalog reference data
 (/usr/share/netinsight/docs/perm_catalog_v1.csv), and the Phase-1
 cinematic installer package (/usr/share/netinsight/installer/) plus
 the /usr/sbin/netinsight-install and /usr/sbin/netinsight-doctor
 launchers.
 .
 The cinematic installer renders a branded TUI (banner, animated data-
 plane workflow, eight-stage progress checklist, final summary card with
 QR) and replaces the raw apt firehose previously shown during install.
 Tier-1 path:  dpkg -i netinsight-release_*.deb && netinsight-install.
 The legacy `apt install netinsight` (Tier-2) path remains supported.
 .
 python3-rich is required for the TUI layout/live primitives.  qrencode
 produces the ANSI256 QR of the GUI URL in the summary card.  figlet,
 boxes, and lolcat are recommended as a degraded ASCII fallback path on
 terminals that cannot render the rich panels.
 .
 This package is required by all other NETINSIGHT binaries.

